# halfcenter -- THE PRODUCED F1 TRAJECTORY. The alternation DOES reach the formant.
# 2026-09-18. verify PASS, pinned hash ad96f882becbee92.
#
# WHY THIS RUN EXISTS: the half-center was put inside the F1 group so the two halves'
# alternation would move the rate-weighted centroid. Five runs measured neural
# anti-phase, within-half coherence, the amplitude envelope and F1 MEANS -- and none
# recorded produced F1 as a TIME SERIES, which is the output.
#
# THE MEANS ALREADY CARRIED IT. The settled-winner arms read F1 438 and 813 Hz; the
# centroid extremes for a 126-neuron, 9-group module are 437.5 and 812.5. So the two
# competing postures ARE the ends of the F1 range and a full alternation is a 375 Hz
# NEURAL swing -- larger than the ~230 Hz absolute naming has always been short of.
#
# THE RESULT, read against a control with both mechanisms OFF (sd 20.9, swing 67.9):
#
#   arm      alt Hz   |H|     predicted   observed swing   excess over control
#   tau083   2.83     0.070    26.3 Hz      47.3 Hz         -20.6 Hz
#   tau167   1.25     0.157    58.9 Hz      74.8 Hz          +6.9 Hz
#   tau250   2.31     0.086    32.2 Hz     106.9 Hz         +39.0 Hz
#   tau333   1.00     0.195    73.2 Hz     135.6 Hz         +67.7 Hz
#
# The two SLOWEST arms land on the pole's prediction (+39.0 vs 32.1; +67.7 vs 73.2),
# and the slower the alternation the more survives -- which is what a low-pass does.
# tau333 free-running produces 135.6 Hz of F1 swing against the control's 67.9: an
# extra 67.7 Hz of articulatory excursion with NO CAREGIVER PRESENT.
#
# MY ZERO-LAG COHERENCE STATISTIC WAS INVALID AND NEARLY COST THE RESULT. A one-pole
# filter phase-shifts by atan(2*pi*f*tau), which at these rates is 79-86 degrees, so
# the zero-lag correlation is capped at cos(lag) = 0.195 / 0.157 / 0.086 / 0.070.
